{"hits": {"hits": [{"links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/190275?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/190275?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/190275?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/190275?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/190275?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/190275?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A190275"}, "metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Jaffe, R.L."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "229", "page_end": "230", "year": 1983, "page_start": "205", "journal_title": "Nucl.Phys.B"}], "texkeys": ["Jaffe:1983hp"], "imprints": [{"date": "1983"}], "abstracts": [{"value": "All O(1/ Q 2 ) corrections to leptoproduction are described by a small number of generalized multiparton distribution functions which depend only on the longitudinal momentum of the partons. We show that these functions can be represented (in A + = 0 gauge) by sequential emission or absorption by the target of quarks, antiquarks and gluons where (i) all quanta move with 0 \u2a7d k + / p + \u2a7d 1; (ii) all intermediate hadronic states are on-mass-shell; (iii) no graphs are semi-disconnected with respect to the target or the intermediate hadronic state. We show how all O(1/ Q 2 ) corrections to the forward virtual Compton amplitude can be represented in terms of these parton distributions."}], "control_number": 190275, "dois": [{"value": "10.1016/0550-3213(83)90361-9"}], "titles": [{"title": "Parton Distribution Functions for Twist Four"}], "author_count": 1, "document_type": ["article"]}, "updated": "2023-03-07T02:06:48.027790+00:00", "id": "190275", "created": "1983-05-01T00:00:00+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Nucl.Phys.B%2C229%2C205&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.